5^{k-1}, so mod 5^4 = 625 it's 4*5^3 = 500). 2016 mod 500 = 16. 2^16 = 65536. 65536 mod 625: 625*104 = 65000, 65536-65000 = 536. ✓\n\nCRT: x ≡ 0 mod 4, x ≡ 536 mod 625. 536 = 4*134, so 536 ≡ 0 mod 4. So x = 536. ✓\n\nA = 536 - 1 = 535 mod 2500. ✓\n\nB: period sum = 250, 100 periods = 25000, plus 16 extra = 185. B = 25185. B mod 2500 = 185. ✓\n\nA - B mod 2500 = 535 - 185 = 350. ✓\n\nS mod 100 = 350/25 = 14. ✓\n\nSo the answer is 14.\n\nLet me verify with small cases. Let me check the formula for a small range.\n\nFor i=0 to 19 (one period): S = sum floor(2^i/25).\n2^i values: 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768,65536,131072,262144,524288.\nfloor(/25): 0,0,0,0,0,1,2,5,10,20,40,81,163,327,655,1310,2621,5242,10485,20995.\n\nSum: 0+0+0+0+0+1+2+5+10+20+40+81+163+327+655+1310+2621+5242+10485+20995.\n= 1+2+5+10+20+40+81+163+327+655+1310+2621+5242+10485+20995\n= (1+2)=3, +5=8, +10=18, +20=38, +40=78, +81=159, +163=322, +327=649, +655=1304, +1310=2614, +2621=5235, +5242=10477, +10485=20962, +20995=41957.\n\nNow using formula: A = 2^20 - 1 = 1048575. B = 250. (A-B)/25 = (1048575-250)/25 = 1048325/25 = 41933.\n\nHmm, that gives 41933, but direct computation gives 41957. Discrepancy of 24. Let me recheck.\n\nWait, for i=0 to 19, that's 20 terms, which is exactly one period. Let me recompute.\n\nActually wait, the issue: A = sum_{i=0}^{19} 2^i = 2^20 - 1 = 1048575. B = sum_{i=0}^{19} r_i = 250. S = (1048575 - 250)/25 = 1048325/25 = 41933.\n\nBut direct sum of floor(2^i/25) for i=0..19 = 41957. These don't match. Let me recheck my direct computation.\n\nfloor(2^10/25) = floor(1024/25) = 40 (1024/25 = 40.96). ✓\nfloor(2^11/25) = floor(2048/25) = 81 (2048/25 = 81.92). ✓\nfloor(2^12/25) = floor(4096/25) = 163 (4096/25 = 163.84). ✓\nfloor(2^13/25) = floor(8192/25) = 327 (8192/25 = 327.68). ✓\nfloor(2^14/25) = floor(16384/25) = 655 (16384/25 = 655.36). ✓\nfloor(2^15/25) = floor(32768/25) = 1310 (32768/25 = 1310.72). ✓\nfloor(2^16/25) = floor(65536/25) = 2621 (65536/25 = 2621.44). ✓\nfloor(2^17/25) = floor(131072/25) = 5242 (131072/25 = 5242.88). ✓\nfloor(2^18/25) = floor(262144/25) = 10485 (262144/25 = 10485.76). ✓\nfloor(2^19/25) = floor(524288/25) = 20995 (524288/25 = 20995.52). ✓\n\nSum of i=10..19: 40+81+163+327+655+1310+2621+5242+10485+20995.\n40+81=121, +163=284, +327=611, +655=1266, +1310=2576, +2621=5197, +5242=10439, +10485=20924, +20995=41919.\n\nSum of i=5..9: 1+2+5+10+20 = 38.\n\nSum of i=0..4: 0.\n\nTotal = 41919 + 38 = 41957.\n\nBut formula gives 41933. Difference = 24.\n\nHmm, so there's an error. Let me recheck the r_i values.\n\nr_i = 2^i mod 25:\ni=0: 1\ni=1: 2\ni=2: 4\ni=3: 8\ni=4: 16\ni=5: 32 mod 25 = 7\ni=6: 64 mod 25 = 14\ni=7: 128 mod 25 = 3 (125 = 5*25, 128-125=3) ✓\ni=8: 256 mod 25 = 6 (250 = 10*25, 256-250=6) ✓\ni=9: 512 mod 25 = 12 (500=20*25, 512-500=12) ✓\ni=10: 1024 mod 25 = 24 (1000=40*25, 1024-1000=24) ✓\ni=11: 2048 mod 25 = 23 (2025=81*25, 2048-2025=23) ✓\ni=12: 4096 mod 25 = 21 (4075=163*25, 4096-4075=21) ✓\ni=13: 8192 mod 25 = 17 (8175=327*25, 8192-8175=17) ✓\ni=14: 16384 mod 25 = 9 (16375=655*25, 16384-16375=9) ✓\ni=15: 32768 mod 25 = 18 (32750=1310*25, 32768-32750=18) ✓\ni=16: 65536 mod 25 = 11 (65525=2621*25, 65536-65525=11) ✓\ni=17: 131072 mod 25 = 22 (131050=5242*25, 131072-131050=22) ✓\ni=18: 262144 mod 25 = 19 (262125=10485*25, 262144-262125=19) ✓\ni=19: 524288 mod 25 = 13 (524275=20971*25, 524288-524275=13). \n\nWait, 20995*25 = 524875, that's bigger than 524288. Let me recompute. 524288/25 = 20971.52. So floor = 20971, not 20995!\n\nLet me recompute floor(2^19/25). 2^19 = 524288. 524288 / 25 = 20971.52. So floor = 20971.\n\nI made an arithmetic error earlier! 524288/25: 25*20000 = 500000, 524288-500000 = 24288. 24288/25 = 971.52. So 20971.52, floor = 20971.\n\nSo floor(2^19/25) = 20971, and 2^19 mod 25 = 524288 - 20971*25 = 524288 - 524275 = 13. ✓ (r_19 = 13 is correct)\n\nLet me redo floor values:\nfloor(2^18/25) = 262144/25 = 10485.76, floor = 10485. 10485*25 = 262125, remain